Original commit body from 31f042d648be92983e0415dc5ebb3ff57a2c19df:

CatalogSpec gains `user_channel` -- the per-family overlay directory under
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/ -- and `no_channel_reason`. Both are REQUIRED
with no default, and that absence is the mechanism rather than an oversight:
a defaulted field would let the next catalogue family silently inherit "no
channel, no reason" and ruling 7 would stop binding. A test pins the
required-ness itself, so a later convenience default fails instead of
quietly disarming the gate.

scripts/yaml-catalog-index --check -- already a CI gate -- now refuses an
incoherent answer, which is what makes the fields mean something rather than
merely exist. Refused: declaring both a channel and a reason for having none;
declaring neither; a channel name that is not <directory>.d (derived, so the
two cannot drift); and channel_scope / channel_gated set on a family with no
channel to apply them to. The shipped registry passes the gate it gained.

All eight families carry their ruling-10 verdict, pinned as a TABLE rather
than a count so a future edit that flips one has to change the test and say
so. Channel: io_primitives, taint_sources, taint_sanitizers (existing),
frameworks (new). No channel: cfg_nodes and url_folding, each with a written
reason -- grammar node types a user cannot know better than, and rows naming
Python engine functions inside the shipped package, which would make a user
file inert without also accepting user code.

Two families needed a qualifier rather than a yes/no:

  dataflow_patterns   channel_scope="library_patterns" -- MIXED. Its grammar
                      rows are internal by the cfg_nodes reasoning; its
                      library_patterns rows are regexes over call syntax that
                      an in-house collection type has a legitimate row to add.
                      Granting the file would hand over the grammar too.
  function_summaries  channel_gated="CAVEAT_USER_SUPPLIED_SANITIZER" -- a
                      terminating user summary IS a sanitizer declaration, so
                      it changes what the tool CLAIMS, not only what it sees.

The CLI and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md both surface the answer, reported PER FAMILY
and not per file: dataflow_patterns' channel is section-scoped and only 9 of
its 20 files carry that section, so "149 of 156 files extensible" would
overstate what a user may actually contribute.

